 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Change delivery via self-hosted WebSockets.** Committed event revisions are pushed to connected browsers across self-hosted WebSocket connections, backed by revision replay for reconnecting clients. HTTPS polling was rejected because of update latency and repeated read traffic. A hosted realtime provider was rejected to avoid recurring vendor fees and third-party operational coupling, accepting server-side connection lifecycle management and client reconnect/catch-up logic. See [`docs/decisions/change-delivery.md`](decisions/change-delivery.md).
